<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ptolemy VI Philometor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 186–145 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ptolemy VI Philometor was king of Ptolemaic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> from 180 to 145 BCE, at times jointly with his brother Ptolemy VIII and his sister-wife Cleopatra II. He survived the invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antiochus-iv-epiphanes">Antiochus IV</a>, which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> halted in 168 BCE, and through Roman arbitration his brother received <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrenaica">Cyrenaica</a> in 163 BCE. He died of wounds in 145 BCE after defeating Alexander Balas in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ptolemy-vi-philometor.jpg" alt="Ptolemy VI Philometor" width="320" height="415" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown artistUnknown artist. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ring_with_engraved_portrait_of_Ptolemy_VI_Philometor_(3rd%E2%80%932nd_century_BCE)_-_2009.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
